      "bottomRightY": 904,
      "content": "1. A Transmitter is permitted to pick any disparity when first transmitting differential data after being in an Electrical Idle state. The Transmitter shall then follow proper 8b/10b encoding rules until the next Electrical Idle state is entered.\n2. The initial disparity for a Receiver is the disparity of the first Symbol used to obtain Symbol lock.\n3. Disparity may also be-reinitialized if Symbol lock is lost and regained during the transmission of differential information due to a burst error event.",
